# Optional settings for scripts/up.sh. Copy to .env and fill in only what
# you need; .env is gitignored. With no .env at all, up.sh still builds the
# whole demo: K8sGPT finds problems and writes Results
#   kubectl --context kind-demo-cluster -n k8sgpt-system get results
# just without AI explanations, and nothing is posted to Slack.
#
# Data sent to the LLM: with an LLM configured, K8sGPT sends what it finds
# in the cluster (resource names, namespaces, events, error messages) to
# the LLM provider to get an explanation. Its anonymize option (on by
# default) masks some object names, but error and event text can still name
# your resources. Only use a provider you are allowed to send that data to,
# or a local model (K8SGPT_LOCAL=true below) to keep it on your machine.

# ─── LLM (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Empty LLM_API_KEY = no AI explanations.
#
# Set LLM_API_KEY to turn them on. The other three are optional:
#   K8SGPT_BACKEND   default openai
#   K8SGPT_MODEL     default gpt-4o-mini
#   K8SGPT_BASE_URL  default empty = the backend's own endpoint
#
# Claude: K8sGPT has no anthropic backend. Keep K8SGPT_BACKEND=openai, use
# an Anthropic key, and set
#   K8SGPT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
#   K8SGPT_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/
#
# Groq free tier (not xAI Grok): create a key at https://console.groq.com,
# then set
#   K8SGPT_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
#   K8SGPT_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# See docs/groq-free-tier-setup.md (repository root) for its limits.
LLM_API_KEY=
K8SGPT_BACKEND=openai
K8SGPT_MODEL=
K8SGPT_BASE_URL=

# ─── Local LLM (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# K8SGPT_LOCAL=true runs K8sGPT against a model served on your machine
# through an OpenAI-compatible API (Ollama by default, or LM Studio, see
# docs/lm-studio.md). Cluster data then stays on your machine. No key is
# needed: LLM_API_KEY is ignored, the backend is always openai, and up.sh
# stops if K8SGPT_BASE_URL is not a local or private address (e.g. a cloud
# URL left above). Defaults, override above if needed:
#   K8SGPT_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
#   K8SGPT_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# host.docker.internal reaches your machine from inside the kind node
# (Docker Desktop and OrbStack provide it). On Linux without Docker
# Desktop, use the Docker bridge IP, e.g. http://172.17.0.1:11434/v1.
K8SGPT_LOCAL=false

# ─── Slack (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slack incoming webhook URL (https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks).
# With it, K8sGPT posts each new Result to that channel; check it with
# ./scripts/check-slack.sh. Empty = no Slack: Results stay in the cluster.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
